  "details": "When you have an avatar or accessory that utilizes a lot of blendshapes you end up having to use a lot of parameter space for things like alternative animations, conditions etc.\n\nIt would be nice with a Blendshape driver or something feature that could read what the current blendshape value is set to and translate that over that to an Animator Controller parameter or directly be used in a transition condition.\n\nWith this you could have a condition right in the FX layer based of what the current blendshape value is without needing a whole animation and synced float value to determinate this.\n\nThis is especially useful for scenarios where you have say a body blendshapes or other things that you wish to only be set once in Unity and not modify ingame.\n\nThis would allow people to create assets that are much more user friendly that don't require them to use up unneeded parameter space, or have to manually tweak an Animator Controller parameter value.",
